cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Chaos, its route, and displacement sensitivity in the quasi-steady falling-plate model"
abstract: >-
  A validated computational study of the two-dimensional quasi-steady falling-plate model
  (Andersen, Pesavento & Wang, 2005) in its thin-card limit: confirmation and delimitation of a
  chaotic band, characterisation of the (non-Feigenbaum) route to chaos, a quantitative link
  between the Lyapunov exponent and landing-displacement sensitivity, and the absence of
  multistability.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rao
    given-names: "M. Subhan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4547-141X"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/sub7an/falling-plate-chaos"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sub7an/falling-plate-chaos"
keywords:
  - falling plate
  - fluttering
  - tumbling
  - deterministic chaos
  - Lyapunov exponent
  - 0-1 test
  - route to chaos
  - nonlinear dynamics
